  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is absent from the verbal report. The individual did not consider the distribution of probabilities or evaluate whether one lottery has a greater probability on the favorable outcome (i.e., non-zero). Instead, the individual only considered the monetary amounts. The decision reason requires an assessment of skewness—specifically, whether a greater portion of probability is assigned to favorable outcomes. Since no such assessment was made, and the individual's justification is based solely on the amount of money (not the distribution), the decision reason was not used. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
