  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not present in the lotteries — both are right-skewed, so no lottery is left-skewed, and thus the reason does not apply. The individual’s deliberation process is based on the probability of winning (25% vs. 20%), not on skewness. There is no mention of skewness, favorable vs. unfavorable probability distribution, or any consideration of the shape of the outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason about skewness. The reason is inapplicable to the problem, and the reported justification does not reference it. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
