  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — specifically, the probability assigned to the favorable (0 Euro) outcome versus the loss — is not mentioned or considered by the individual. The individual only discusses the probability of losing, without comparing the favorable vs. unfavorable outcome probabilities. The decision reason requires evaluating skewness (i.e., the proportion of probability on favorable outcomes) to determine preference. Since the individual does not reference skewness or the distributional shape of the lotteries, nor does the individual apply the rule that prefers the more left-skewed lottery (which would be Lottery B), the decision reason was not used. The justification given is about the risk of loss being low, which is a different criterion (risk aversion or risk tolerance), not skewness-based reasoning. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

